ones, having in distress arrived at the river Mandākini, Mandākini, having convenient descents, charming, ever furnished with blossomag woods, and of rapid currents; and approached it descents, goodly and void of mud, offered water to the monarch, uttering, “May this be so!\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.647,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f2836533a15dcaa4b935a35a5054ccddabc97e84d065860f8f912ae7c1d6f7be","compact":"5a60e76b446dbd3a8fccf6c9e53a4a0bfdc33124317946bd4b9ba3bc155629ab","nasal":"f6406081be500fc1a81a41416ecbcfddeba52de2f368cc62e81e8db3df1d248d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":26,"english":"Then those illustrious ones, having in distress arrived at the river Mandākini, Mandākini, having convenient descents, charming, ever furnished with blossomag woods, and of rapid currents; and approached it descents, goodly and void of mud, offered water to the monarch, uttering, “May this be so!\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4e9c7808469b80124f49b6a9d547cfbfab26d48695b62f458db410df1827d836","compact":"680f52a688561e6d6244ef65ac0dfcb2e8e2b9907b8d20fb84131c54909292ca","nasal":"680f52a688561e6d6244ef65ac0dfcb2e8e2b9907b8d20fb84131c54909292ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":27,"english":"The protector of the earth (Rama), holding water with his joined hands, facing the south, said weeping, “O foremost of monarchs, may this clear water knowing no deterioration, reach you, who have gone to the world of the ancestral manes.!\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.737,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"694698d08349b8278df55392fa31a058f089930f08893e2ebc6b5e7988a81cf0","compact":"8a0d76199e3dc72c1bfe6a2579cbd7653e83e11e009da833af8d498a3f637c1e","nasal":"e767092c472ddbf4c20c5a932aa2f806c0f26d57dd54db54ef2006cf64a2943e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":28,"english":"The protector of the earth (Rama), holding water with his joined hands, facing the south, said weeping, “O foremost of monarchs, may this clear water knowing no deterioration, reach you, who have gone to the world of the ancestral manes.!\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba5a9740b748666ac78a0d6ca2c86532ce6d88281539c6fe0ab55f858bebf77b","compact":"63263c7616caff59975a8e7d030abdc19d59f49b6fc268de53a6527dee78b63e","nasal":"f6b4dff2418a57b6f31caeddd5f65bbaae82d37ce57a958553a5e0cb9792ecfd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":29,"english":"Then drawing nigh to the marge of the Mandākinī, the energetic Rāghava along with his brothers, offered the Pinda to his father.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"379ea44501fd3b3aeb1c925990573d007a5c1de0a2c75b1061fb86b0f775a6ad","compact":"39a81b4539a31207a4db26c189d531bf88f223283a3f6885689f5ecb01e10588","nasal":"98e267c3a63c598b2587e338306c2f0a9bf8d39ee447362e000339091b746daa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":30,"english":"And placing the Ingudi Pinda mixed with jujube on a bed of darbha, Rāma crying in distress, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c32078ea91bf3d3b16ef6e597d8fde8e968f286ea88461b71ad1335b4780280c","compact":"bba4fc9e72637c0a5ff6af8cbf6e143138d74e5282a03c2cff1fd7bfb9831732","nasal":"4ffb4cf5b9d5a9f4c291a1567c7c4e5ad00910245b2a8d2da1bd154a52b35a69"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":31,"english":"O mighty monarch! do you well pleased feed on this, which we also live upon. That which is the fare of an individual, is also the fare of his divinities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"97f0661cfb1e5a804cb5e546347d965a87b597d78806ff8ad782f4b898215ff8","compact":"449be7117ce72859a9c13d197d0f3ac41a7ceeaebde1e504510c97217b5da2fb","nasal":"867f264d085989a243c5239c155edff2edfaf60d835bf9d5afebd58ecdc5c2d2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":32,"english":"Then that forernost of men ascending the bank of the stream by the self-same way, got up on the charming side of the hill. And having arrived at the gate of the cottage of leaves, that lord of the earth held both Bharata and Laksmana with his hands.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"565d78df42d197fccd2c38607a1e8d61b6fb97f643cb64f3c502ac6983ed9c15","compact":"c00bea5bdebb6ad1eca45f2ae7ae9a7d93eae942f1a061a1100d55edbeaec23e","nasal":"c00bea5bdebb6ad1eca45f2ae7ae9a7d93eae942f1a061a1100d55edbeaec23e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":33,"english":"Then that forernost of men ascending the bank of the stream by the self-same way, got up on the charming side of the hill. And having arrived at the gate of the cottage of leaves, that lord of the earth held both Bharata and Laksmana with his hands.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"441e6ec834408a3e12e547309818bb679663b9704e58e573abc5f7567ff8adec","compact":"e3027cc269053da9b65589cf33493dc1e5e75d0391c3467ba48b6ad6dbccf5a2","nasal":"e3027cc269053da9b65589cf33493dc1e5e75d0391c3467ba48b6ad6dbccf5a2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":34,"english":"And there the hill reverberated at the sounds raised by the brothers wailing along with Vaidehi; like to lions roaring.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.686,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f485d91a414dab0c6b350d35f14293a0336f82f6c5868182fa0ebe31748073b6","compact":"def7d3891ddc1a8daf6eb1d2e81999906376cbc19c0c43c855f4b1de9524d226","nasal":"def7d3891ddc1a8daf6eb1d2e81999906376cbc19c0c43c855f4b1de9524d226"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":35,"english":"And perceiving the loud uproar of those mighty ones engaged in offering water to their sire, indulging in lamentations, the army of Bharata became agitated. And they said, “For certain Bharata has met with Rāma; and this mighty noise proceeds from them, as they are bitterly mourning their deceased sire.”","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.905,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f6b8ed75c6a06104418a69818010b5f5a055bd987106a71c1ec9b1f69e88ec94","compact":"75c39bfd8907839b39abceabb2bb246dd7928823d76f5cf5e059d4fa137614d3","nasal":"75c39bfd8907839b39abceabb2bb246dd7928823d76f5cf5e059d4fa137614d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":36,"english":"Thereat leaving aside their vehicles, they with one mind, rushed towards the spot wherefrom proceeded the uproar.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.909,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"764e485c797c125d7aa90bbd9dad18f8f1e78e84e07d9b771693ea00977f3247","compact":"d50b48bd72b9744c1044c6583d50350d8aa859ec42da2c7ab7f8bcd766d9c23e","nasal":"d50b48bd72b9744c1044c6583d50350d8aa859ec42da2c7ab7f8bcd766d9c23e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-37","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":37,"english":"And of those that were tender, some went on horses, and some on elephants, and some on ornamented chariots, while others went on foot.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095037","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c2ea645b7a60697f288e10509430350e28cb56aef10aa67ea468539f77b312a6","compact":"f3062dc9b86d97fb71eb015defef098b5f5f2217158cbf026e6212364f315f4d","nasal":"f3062dc9b86d97fb71eb015defef098b5f5f2217158cbf026e6212364f315f4d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-38","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":38,"english":"And eager to behold Rāma staying away for a short time though seeming to do so for a long period, all the men at once went to the hermitage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095038","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1a78c3866b5b5892a0e1d18990ca1e637d94abb4b38a9658620697f6db3ed153","compact":"372a5f8b4ba3167241447b744b8734859a1bf19f533bf9571ea56e48696fb6c9","nasal":"372a5f8b4ba3167241447b744b8734859a1bf19f533bf9571ea56e48696fb6c9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-39","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":39,"english":"And desirous of witnessing the meeting of the brothers (with Rāma), they with all despatch proceeded by means of various vehicles consisting of beasts and cars.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.912,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095039","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1a2a467fd1bcfa806f5d574c5e79a6e592f837a8eab52da6fe04262a9ba0b0fc","compact":"d9530599e7f0d57ea606cd8c1af1b7131898d12c4a8d19c67f005f89158f7b0d","nasal":"d9530599e7f0d57ea606cd8c1af1b7131898d12c4a8d19c67f005f89158f7b0d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-40","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":40,"english":"And the ground trodden by the wheels of innumerable cars, emitted loud sounds, like those emitted by the sky on clouds gathering.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095040","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8960011babcabd9054feded05a4f1610c0305e6405e6a12df51f8819d3c4e24","compact":"db591f0d57a4a0165fea46a9654f6814413b94243f628fba49eb367d6023297e","nasal":"db591f0d57a4a0165fea46a9654f6814413b94243f628fba49eb367d6023297e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-41","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":41,"english":"And frightened by the uproar, elephants accompanied by female ones, perfuming all sides (by the fragrance of temporal juice), went to another forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095041","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f70ffe1f1dd96002dd52de3101c7988316cafaf79577ecb6ce80e5076be1e9f1","compact":"db3e72e114dfdc4701839320cf0ec6c8f298e215148e68473010443a18cd73f5","nasal":"7d27d4c914a7f79e88d1eb07132ecd1786b5d0160024b0f74b8633e308ceea26"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-42","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":42,"english":"And boars, and deer, and lions, and buffaloes, and Srmaras, and tigers, and Gokarnas, Gavayas and Prşatas were stricken with panic.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.45,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095042","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f59b52b1469be99eb96e6cf7272cb2c97b1140ed2d85de9567721c624837945a","compact":"87cdce8d19bbfadeb9199964a078913fd0d2df9432b54cc4604cb657212287f8","nasal":"87cdce8d19bbfadeb9199964a078913fd0d2df9432b54cc4604cb657212287f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-43","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":43,"english":"And wild with alarm, Chakravakas, and swans, and Natyuhas, and Plavas, and Karandavas, and male coels, and Kraunchas, fled away in all directions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.548,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095043","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a41993fe685d6b7367d33ea0e5762c8a2b48a5e8b97857a5cf7df54b8bed6213","compact":"69c0dde2b58db679ed3c93f03ab1a405516fdaa8e072c72f6241c8b7ff90b9a4","nasal":"61a5cae5ef20d7b0f33268c242953624cf15f32056165884c633fa9211160292"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-44","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":44,"english":"And the welkin was enveloped by birds frightened by the noise, as the earth was covered by men, and both the sky and the land then gave out great effulgence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095044","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f260c5ce626de8c3d5098bb7f2156a178e37457af170d41c3e49f6e3fcdedf7f","compact":"b1d271a77aac58d179a7c9131bc0077bca84ffd592cca875cb5c261235ec7ba9","nasal":"20b69325ff5e0291ebdf0efae4e78726f282fb931a86e1cd0035db9b9bc0ff2a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-45","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":45,"english":"Seeing those men oppressed with grief with their eyes filled with tears, that one cognizant of virtue like fathers and mothers, embraced those that deserved it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095045","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd556f7d9cfeef61755cd8f5ee601ea89e39f4223f527f3f68e7308f246d6db7","compact":"a520acd72516df6540525597858d48ad48edb8f2c8560b16be076145ec3f6ae3","nasal":"e8e209ab9d6ab0c6276eba03a00b4f1b968fe1a5a9077722a31566effbe20f68"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-46","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":46,"english":"And he embraced some persons; and some offered him salutations. And the king's son, as each deserved, properly received them along with their friends and equals in age.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095046","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cb1903ff255a75dbd4a14d83e277330e861ad64807a84fd64b65300dc1860a9e","compact":"ed84f646b5756c385a1a5e99dc66f58229f84640221acd77e10bb5e3daa4212b","nasal":"ebe91e929a75865859c80c693de0dd00ecf30e735de3df5eeb1da19a047ee7d0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-95-47","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":95,"verse":47,"english":"And the sounds, produced by those high souled persons lamenting, resounding the earth and the sky, and the mountain-caverns, and all the cardinal points, were heard like peals of Mrdangas. And the sounds, produced by those high souled persons lamenting, resounding the earth and the sky, and the mountain-caverns, and all the cardinal points, were heard like peals of Mrdangas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-103-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2095047","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fe058d695614b5e9ab74bb2c6ae51b77fe37a13c02e859ebf2a8ef15a3ed4414","compact":"14bf2137780d592dcf7f9480d5a845b2e614698140aa6b18a433c4f8dafe59d3","nasal":"f17a458e51dd264d139f50dfd2aaa6ad4fcb3671a72caff30ff8ff5f2aa15827"}}]
